{
  "type": "output_text",
  "text": {
    "value": "Based on the web results, there is no direct public documentation or prominent open-source code reference specifically for \"visitGraphQLDirective\" or \"visitGraphQLAppliedDirective\" methods in combination with a \"GraphQLTypeVisitor\" interface or class. However, there is a clear and well-known pattern in the [graphql-java](https://github.com/graphql-java/graphql-java) library and similar GraphQL libraries involving type visitor interfaces and directive handling.\n\n**Context from graphql-java:**\n\n- `GraphQLTypeVisitor` is an interface commonly used for traversing elements of a GraphQL schema in Java. Methods like `visitGraphQLFieldDefinition` and similar are standard in the graphql-java library for visiting parts of the schema【3:2†source】.\n- Handling directives (i.e., things like `visitGraphQLDirective`) typically happens within the context of schema transformation or analysis, but it appears neither the official docs nor GitHub issues reference a method exactly named `visitGraphQLDirective` or `visitGraphQLAppliedDirective` as of now.\n- The pattern might be familiar if you're building or extending tools around schema generation, transformation, or federation, where custom visitor methods could be added to handle directive nodes on schema elements.\n\n**If you're developing your own schema visitor:**\n- You might extend or implement `GraphQLTypeVisitor` and create methods like `visitGraphQLDirective` for custom processing of `GraphQLDirective` schema elements.\n- Here’s a conceptual pattern:\n    ```java\n    public interface GraphQLTypeVisitor {\n        TraversalControl visitGraphQLFieldDefinition(GraphQLFieldDefinition fieldDef, TraverserContext\u003cGraphQLSchemaElement\u003e context);\n        // Your own extension, for example:\n        TraversalControl visitGraphQLDirective(GraphQLDirective directive, TraverserContext\u003cGraphQLSchemaElement\u003e context);\n    }\n    ```\n- In actual [graphql-java](https://github.com/graphql-java/graphql-java), you would implement or extend the `GraphQLTypeVisitorStub` or similar classes and add your own directive-specific logic.\n\n**Summary:**  \n- There are no built-in methods called `visitGraphQLDirective` or `visitGraphQLAppliedDirective` in the most-used libraries as of mid-2024.\n- `GraphQLTypeVisitor` is a real pattern in graphql-java and can be customized to walk and process the schema, including directives【3:2†source】.\n- Extending the visitor with your own directive-visit methods is a reasonable approach for schema transformations or code generation use cases.\n\nIf you have a very specific codebase or library in mind (other than graphql-java), please provide its name for tailored examples! Otherwise, you may need to implement such visiting logic yourself in Java or the relevant language.",
